#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#A VS solver program can be loaded and run from a MATLAB M-file. This example is described in a tech memo accessed from Help > Technical Memos > Example: Automating Runs with the VS API.
#
#If you want to use the feature which allows you to save multiple sets of results, the ring control must be set prior generating the files for the run.
#
#To make the run:
#1. Click the button "Generate Files for this Run",
#2. From within MATLAB, run the file "Simple.m" from the folder Extensions\Custom_M.
#
#For 64-bit MATLAB, please change the linked Model dataset to the 64-bit example. Be aware that a MATLAB-compatible external C compiler is required to use the MATLAB loadlibrary function for 64-bit MATLAB.
#
#Note that this simulation is overlaid with the Quick Start Guide, Baseline example to demonstrate that the simulation results to do not differ between running the M-file and the baseline example.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

